# Self-hosted JSON import boundary

The native v2 lane exposes strict parsing, typed navigation, lookup, and
rendering through the explicitly imported `std/json.ssc` facade. JSON null is
the portable Unit value and fractional tokens remain exact Decimals. Legacy
plugin-global fixtures exercise a different API and are not evidence for this
boundary.

[jsonParse, jsonRead, jsonStringify, lookup, lookupOpt](std/json.ssc)

```scalascript
val parsedNull: Any = jsonParse("null")
val parsedDecimal: Any = jsonParse("0.0")
println(parsedNull)
println(parsedDecimal)
println(jsonStringify(parsedNull))
println(jsonStringify(parsedDecimal))

val wrapped = jsonRead("""{"name":"Ada","count":2}""")
println(wrapped("name").asString)
println(wrapped("count").asInt)
println(wrapped.get("missing"))

val raw: Any = jsonParse("""{"name":"Ada"}""")
println(lookup(raw, "name"))
println(lookupOpt(raw, "missing"))

println(jsonStringify(List(1, 2, 3)))
```
